Riksarkivet/universalviewer4 at UV4_REF (.docker/htrflow-web.dockerfile),
patched for the web image. Generated as a `git diff` in a clone on that
commit; `git apply` skips this preamble. What each file changes:

- uv.html: fetch uv-iiif-config.json through the configure event (without
  it textRightPanelEnabled stays false and the ALTO panel never shows). A
  #?config= is honoured on the page's own origin only: UV writes a
  config's content strings into the page as HTML.
- TextRightPanel.ts: scale ALTO coords to the displayed image and convert
  them to viewport coords; and render ALTO line text (and search-hit text)
  as text, never as HTML, so a line reading <img src=x onerror=...> is
  shown, not run on the web front's origin (2026-09-17 audit, 3059).
- TextRightPanel.ts (also): draw each line's outline, its ALTO
  TextLine/Shape/Polygon, as an svg polygon inside the line's overlay div
  (built as DOM nodes from points parsed as finite numbers); a line with
  no usable Polygon keeps its bounding box. The div, and so the hit area,
  stays the bounding box.
- TextRightPanel.ts (also): show the page's predicted quality, ALTO
  Page/@PC as htrflow's QualityPrediction writes it, under the header --
  read off the same ALTO as the lines, set as text.
- SearchLeftPanel.ts: render the search service's hit text (before, match,
  after) as text too; with a manifest from anywhere, its search service is
  as untrusted as its ALTO.
- OpenSeadragonCenterPanel.ts: re-add the current canvas's line overlays
  after clearOverlays(), in viewport coords.
- styles.less: outline the line overlays; a line with a polygon carries
  its outline and fill (the current-line highlight too) on the polygon, in
  a stroke that stays thin at any zoom.

